## Introduction
This tutorial provides step-by-step guidance for student event organizers to design an event poster and export it as a PDF file using the web version of Canva.

## Step 1: Access and log into Canva
1. Open your web browser and go to the official Canva website.
2. Log in with your email address. New users can sign up for a free account.
3. You will arrive at the Canva homepage with template resources.

## Step 2: Start a new poster design
1. Click **Create a design** on the top-right corner.
2. Choose a poster size such as A4 or A3, or set a custom size.
3. A blank canvas will load for your poster design.

## Step 3: Select a template and edit content
1. Browse the template library on the left and pick a suitable event poster template.
2. Replace the sample text with your event information: event title, speaker, time, location and registration details.
3. Adjust font, colour and text alignment to keep information easy to read.
4. Add icons or simple graphics if needed. Avoid overcrowding the layout.

## Step 4: Preview your poster
1. Check the whole poster carefully. Look for typos, missing information or layout problems.
2. Modify any mistakes before export.

## Step 5: Export the poster as PDF
1. Click the **Share** button at the top right.
2. Select **Download** from the dropdown menu.
3. Set the file type to **PDF Standard**.
4. Click Download. The PDF file will save to your local device.

## Troubleshooting
If the download fails, check your internet connection or try a different browser.
If images look blurry, make sure you select high-quality export settings.
